{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787796019812480001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"beton-inversive-stag","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"69d50697d04173c3a2afff8f5f3b7d8fdda283edd845bdda6ac84bf41f1f7f91","event_uuid":"9f80b3f8-1a30-4143-8528-6a99e48b7dbd","position":{"commit_sha":"1e0add92d0ea2560143e0f4382d1c12317992198","position":"1787773101245614001-9f80b3f8-1a30-4143-8528-6a99e48b7dbd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5c8dbf5d776248a9a076212883cbf1c56ac81daaf2f9bfa6ea6df4b81fe3cf0c","event_uuid":"752d8402-562e-4192-a7f5-47ce7c4561bf","position":{"commit_sha":"f68b07e28aa0cfd30da3988cef38eaba24b157e8","position":"1787773138186581001-752d8402-562e-4192-a7f5-47ce7c4561bf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787773101245614001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"752d8402-562e-4192-a7f5-47ce7c4561bf","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d467-e2fc-fd64-49ae"}],"description":"MCP containers start through launch paths that take NO deploy mutex, so the\nautodeploy `flock` cannot be relied on to serialize anything the entrypoint does.\n\nEvidence (found while remediating Gerrit 2244 / d467-e2fc-fd64-49ae):\n\n1. `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:324` — the `mcp:` service is `restart: always`\n   and mounts `gerrit_mcp_tickets:/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` (line 399), the SAME\n   named volume `mcp_run_new` mounts (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:370`). A docker\n   daemon restart, host reboot, or crash-loop re-runs the ENTRYPOINT with no flock.\n   The compose file itself (lines 391-393) documents an expected crash-loop when\n   `mcp-static-tokens.json` is absent.\n2. The compose service pins host 8091, which is inside the managed port pool\n   {8091, MCP_PORT_A, MCP_PORT_B} with `MCP_RELEASES_CAP=3`\n   (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:129,136`), so it can coexist with blue/green\n   containers on the same volume.\n3. Operator runbook restarts (`infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`) are a further\n   unserialized launch path.\n4. Even WITHIN autodeploy the flock does not cover provisioning: it is backgrounded\n   and outlives the tick (/health answers before the store exists — see the separate\n   open bug mobile-groovy-badger), so the 2-minute timer can start a second container\n   while the first is still cloning.\n\nRe-clone concurrency specifically IS now handled: 2244 adds a hard-link lock in\n`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` covering clear+clone across containers. This ticket\ntracks the RESIDUAL, more general risk: the deploy mutex is not a serialization\nguarantee for the entrypoint, so any FUTURE entrypoint step that mutates the shared\nvolume must carry its own serialization, and nothing currently enforces or documents\nthat expectation.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- The unserialized launch paths above are documented where an author of the entrypoint\n  will see them (entrypoint header comment and/or an infra runbook), stating that the\n  deploy flock does not serialize entrypoint work.\n- A decision is recorded on whether the compose `mcp:` service should keep\n  `restart: always` on 8091 while blue/green containers manage the same volume, or be\n  reduced to a boot-only backend.\n- If the answer is that further steps need serialization, the lock is factored so a new\n  step can reuse it rather than re-inventing one.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","mcp","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"1890-7d05-eabc-4ac1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP entrypoint launch paths bypass the autodeploy deploy mutex","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9f80b3f8-1a30-4143-8528-6a99e48b7dbd","752d8402-562e-4192-a7f5-47ce7c4561bf"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787796019812480001,"uuid":"a0948494-0715-4e7b-9c10-cc217ec144b1"}